<title>FRANCE: French producer prices seen stable in Q2 - survey.</title>
<headline>French producer prices seen stable in Q2 - survey.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>French producer prices for manufactured goods are expected to stabilise in the second quarter after falling a seasonally adjusted 0.6 percent in the first quarter, national statistics institute INSEE said on Tuesday in its quarterly survey of industry.</p>
<p>It gave the following figures for output prices, by percentage change from previous quarter (seasonally adjusted unless stated)</p>
<p>					     Q297    Q197    Q496     Q396</p>
<p>PRICE CHANGE OF PVS QUARTER</p>
<p>  -- Manufacturing industry	   =	-0.6     0.1     -0.6</p>
<p>  -- Total industry (unadj)	   =	-0.2    -0.2     -0.3</p>
<p>PRICE CHANGE EXPECTED NEXT QUARTER</p>
<p>  -- Manufacturing industry	 -0.1     -0.2    -0.2     -0.2</p>
<p>  -- Total industry		    0.0     -0.2    -0.1     -0.2</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5381</p>
</text>
